					'This is a fixed pairing, not a free choice: the *si*-clause cannot take the present subjunctive or the conditional itself when the hypothesis is contrary to present fact, and the main clause cannot take the present or future indicative there either. [The imperfect subjunctive on the *si* side is the same mood the subjunctive uses](/subjunctive-spanish/) whenever a clause needs to mark something as unreal or unverified rather than asserted. The conditional in the main clause is simply what completes that unreal framing on the outcome side.',
