				answer: "No, the vast majority get by without one, since ordinary Spanish spelling signals stress on its own. The exceptions are words whose stress falls somewhere the ending wouldn't predict, words that carry a tilde every single time with no exceptions (esdrújulas and their rarer cousins, sobresdrújulas), and the small set of monosyllables where only a tilde can tell a word apart from its identical twin.",
